<div style="border: 2px solid #1a5276; padding: 15px; text-align: center; background-color: #e0f2f7; margin-bottom: 20px;">
    <h1 style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # Our Community News – Lesson # 5</h1>
    <p style="color: #1a5276; margin: 5px 0 0 0;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 5</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Mediation</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 6th Grade (CEFR: A2.1)</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> Our Community News</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> Reporting From the School!</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
            <b>Specific Objective:</b>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Mediation: text_1: Write simple interpretations of common texts in English supported with visual aids.
            text_2: Explain the main points of class readings to peers.</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
            <b>Learning Outcome:</b>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Mediation: Can write simple summaries of community news articles with visual support (e.g., uses an image of the parade as an aid for the summary, 'The Desfile de las Mil Polleras took place last weekend. Many women wore colorful polleras and danced in the streets.').
            Can explain the main points of class readings about Panamanian traditions using visuals (e.g., shows pictures of Carnival floats and attendees while explaining, 'The text talks about Carnival in Chitré. People enjoy the parades and music.').
            Can simplify event flyers for peers, highlighting key details with visuals (e.g., 'The school fair is on Friday at 9 a.m.' with a drawing of a calendar and school, or 'The Fiestas Patrias parade starts at 10 a.m.' with a picture of a marching band').</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276; text-align: center;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tr style="background-color: #f2f2f2;">
        <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 30%; color: #1a5276;">Stage & Description</th>
        <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%; color: #1a5276;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
        <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 20%; color: #1a5276;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
    </tr>

    <tr>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</b></p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Engagement, Modeling and Clarification)</p>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher shows images of various community events (e.g., a school fair, a local parade, a community mural project). Students briefly recall the events from previous lessons and say one thing they remember or liked about each, using the past simple tense. Example: "I remember the colorful parade last year." or "The students prepared a mural about the Desfile de las Mil Polleras."</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher holds up a simple, made-up news headline and a picture from a local event (e.g., "School Fair Was a Great Success!"). The teacher then models how to explain the news simply to the class: "Last Saturday, our school celebrated a community fair. It was a very friendly event. Many people participated. I liked the games, but I didn't like the long lines for food." The teacher explicitly highlights the use of past simple and descriptive adjectives and practices the pronunciation of past tense -ed endings (/d/ in 'celebrated', /t/ in 'liked').</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b></p>
            <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Did I tell you *all* the tiny details, or just the main idea?" (Expected answer: "Main idea.")</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What did I use to help you understand better?" (Expected answer: "The picture/visual.")</li>
            </ul>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Date] <br> [Time]</p>
        </td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 2 — Presentation</b></p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "Our Community News")</p>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> The teacher presents a short, simple "Community News" article (or an event flyer) from a local school, titled "Chitré School Carnival Parade!". The text includes information about who participated, what they did, when and where it took place, and some descriptions using target vocabulary (e.g., 'colorful Carnival floats,' 'Carnival Queen,' 'students prepared,' 'friendly teachers'). It incorporates past simple tense and adjectives describing physical appearance (e.g., 'The Carnival Queen was tall and had blond, curly hair.'). A picture of the parade is shown alongside the text.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Sharing past experiences and preferences (e.g., 'I went to the Desfile de las Mil Polleras. I liked the different colorful polleras.'), and Describing people and community members (e.g., 'The artisan has curly hair and is very kind.')</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b></p>
            <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students read the article/flyer silently.</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist questions:</b> "What event is the news article about?" "When did it happen?" "Who participated?" (Students answer orally or by pointing to parts of the text).</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>True/False:</b> The teacher reads simple statements based on the text (e.g., "The parade was in the morning." or "The Carnival Queen had straight hair.") and students indicate True or False.</li>
            </ul>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Date] <br> [Time]</p>
        </td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</b></p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Accuracy focus on Mediation)</p>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Students practice mediating information using past simple tense, compound sentences with 'but', descriptive adjectives (colorful, traditional, friendly, tall, slender, chubby, curly hair), and target vocabulary (community, parade, festival, reporter, tradition, Pollera, Carnival float). Focus on pronunciation of past tense -ed endings (/t/, /d/, /ɪd/) and identifying short/long vowel sounds (e.g., /æ/ in 'banner' vs. /eɪ/ in 'parade').</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
            <ul style="list-style-type: decimal; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>"Key Details Summary":</b> In pairs, students use a provided graphic organizer to extract key details (Who, What, Where, When, Why) from the "Chitré School Carnival Parade!" article. Then, they use these details to complete simple sentence frames: "The news article talks about _________." "It happened in _________." "Many students _________." This is a controlled practice for simplifying text.</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>"Simplify a Paragraph":</b> The teacher assigns each pair a paragraph or a specific section of the news article/flyer. Students work together to rewrite 2-3 sentences from their section in simpler terms, imagining they are explaining it to a younger student. They must include at least one past simple verb, one descriptive adjective, and one visual aid (a simple drawing or icon). Example: "The text says many women wore polleras. We can say: 'Women had beautiful dresses!' (with a drawing of a Pollera)."</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>"Peer Explanation & Feedback":</b> Students take turns explaining their simplified section to another pair, showing their visual aid. The listening pair provides feedback on clarity and understanding, gently (e.g., 'I like your explanation, but maybe you can explain "mural" again?'). This activity practices softening disagreement and focuses on the communicative goal of making information clear to others.</li>
            </ul>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Date] <br> [Time]</p>
        </td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</b></p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "Our Community News")</p>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Students will perform the "Community News Report" 21st Century Skills Project, specifically focusing on the mediation aspect by presenting and explaining their report sections.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task format:</b> "Community News Reporters" - Students work in small groups (2-3 students). Each group has prepared a section of their "Community News Report" (e.g., one article about a school event, a short interview with a community member, or a description of a local tradition) with accompanying visuals (drawings, cutouts, simple diagrams). They take turns presenting their section to another group or to the whole class, acting as junior reporters. For each section, they must:</p>
            <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Explain the main points of their news article or description in simple English, using the past simple tense.</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Use their visual aids to support their explanation (e.g., pointing to an image of the parade as they describe it).</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Include at least one compound sentence with 'but' to express a preference or contrasting idea related to the event (e.g., 'I liked the colorful floats, but I didn't like the loud music.').</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Describe at least one person using adjectives of physical appearance if applicable (e.g., 'The Carnival Queen was tall and had blond, curly hair.').</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Answer simple questions from their audience about their report.</li>
            </ul>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Focus:</b> Fluency in explaining, clarity in summarizing, effective use of visuals, collaboration within the group, and accurate use of past simple tense and target vocabulary.</p>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Date] <br> [Time]</p>
        </td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</b></p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Formative assessment strategy)</p>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative assessment strategy:</b> Teacher Observation Checklist and Peer Assessment.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> During their "Community News Reporters" presentations, the teacher uses an observation checklist to note individual and group performance. Peers also use a simple checklist to assess the clarity and effectiveness of the presentations from other groups.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria (Teacher Checklist / Peer Checklist):</b></p>
            <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Explained main points of the news article clearly.</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Used visual aids effectively to support the explanation.</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Used past simple tense correctly (e.g., 'The students prepared a mural.').</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Included at least one sentence with 'but' (e.g., 'I liked the food, but I didn't like the music.').</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Used target vocabulary (e.g., 'community,' 'parade,' 'colorful').</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Pronunciation of past tense -ed endings was intelligible.</li>
            </ul>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students complete the following prompts on a small slip of paper:</p>
            <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"One thing I explained well today was..."</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"My visual aid helped my classmates understand because..."</li>
            </ul>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Date] <br> [Time]</p>
        </td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 6 — Reflection</b></p>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection:</b></p>
            <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What part of explaining my community news report was easy for me today?"</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What did I learn about making information clear to others?"</li>
            </ul>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b></p>
            <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What worked well in the mediation activities? Were students able to effectively simplify information and use visuals to support their explanations?</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What adjustments and scaffolds are needed for students who struggled with expressing their preferences using 'but' or accurately using past simple tense in their explanations? How can I further encourage softening disagreement during peer feedback?</li>
            </ul>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson in the theme sequence:</b> This lesson concludes the "Our Community News" theme. The next lesson will introduce a new theme, building upon the skills of describing past events and mediating information, possibly with a focus on future events or more complex community issues, allowing for further development of communicative competences.</p>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Date] <br> [Time]</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>